-- Generated by rs3-api-types from https://developer.runescape.com/rs/ui/interface.html;
-- regenerate it with ./gradlew generate rather than editing it.

---An interface is essentially a self-contained bundle of components created from packed game assets, and loaded on
---demand by the UI system. Only one top-level interface can be loaded at any one point, with additional sub-interfaces
---being loaded within components in the top-level interface.
---
---It's through interfaces that plugins can access existing components and use them as a parent for plugin components,
---or scan the built-in UI for data that might not yet be exposed in an easier-to-access manner.
---
---Info: Since plugins can't create new interfaces, they must instead use components in the appropriate interface as a
---parent for their components. Using the right interface is important since components only live for as long as their
---interface is loaded.
---
---Warning: Although care is generally taken to avoid changes to built-in interfaces that would result in components
---being removed or changing to a different type over time, plugins should always check any components they obtain are
---valid and of the desired type prior to performing any actions on them. This is particularly important when a plugin
---is accessing or making use of components dynamically created by the built-in interfaces, since the IDs those
---components are associated with do not represent a static target, meaning the type of the component corresponding to
---those IDs could change over time, resulting in potential plugin errors if a specific type is assumed.
---@class ui.Interface
---@field id integer (Read-only) Unique numeric value used to identify this specific interface.
---@field clientOnly boolean (Read-only) True if this interface is managed entirely by the client and doesn't interact with the server.
local Interface = {}

---Attempts to retrieve the component associated with the various provided IDs contained within this interface.
---@param staticID integer ID value used to identify the static component that's being retrieved, or that contains the dynamic component that's being retrieved.
---@return ui.Component?
---@overload fun(self: ui.Interface, staticID: integer, categoryID: integer, dynamicID: integer): ui.Component?
function Interface:GetComponent(staticID) end

---The `ui.Interfaces` object provides helper methods for quickly retrieving loaded interfaces and their components.
---@class ui.Interfaces
ui.Interfaces = {}

---Retrieves the loaded interface matching the specified ID.
---@param interfaceID integer ID value used to identify the interface containing the component that's being retrieved.
---@return ui.Interface? # The interface associated with the specified ID, or nil if missing or not loaded.
function ui.Interfaces:GetInterface(interfaceID) end

---Retrieves the loaded interface matching the specified ID, and searches within for a component associated with the
---various provided IDs.
---
---Info: This is equivalent to retrieving an interface using `ui.Interfaces:GetInterface` and then calling
---`ui.Interface:GetComponent` on it if the interface isn't nil. Prefer using that method instead if the plugin needs to
---retrieve components from the same interface often, as it avoids redundant interface lookups.
---@param combinedID integer The combined ID ( `(interfaceID << 16) | staticID` ) used to identify the component that's being retrieved. Combined IDs are available via lookups such as `id.Component.TOPLEVEL_V2__GAME_AREA` where the double-underscore separates the interface name (`TOPLEVEL_V2`) and the name of the component within it (`GAME_AREA`)
---@return ui.Component? # The component of the appropriate type associated with the specified interface and component IDs, or nil if there's no component with these IDs or the interface isn't loaded.
---@overload fun(self: ui.Interfaces, combinedID: integer, categoryID: integer, dynamicID: integer): ui.Component?
---@overload fun(self: ui.Interfaces, interfaceID: integer, staticID: integer): ui.Component?
---@overload fun(self: ui.Interfaces, interfaceID: integer, staticID: integer, categoryID: integer, dynamicID: integer): ui.Component?
function ui.Interfaces:GetComponent(combinedID) end
